ming alongside the  new iphones at the september event  and i'm very confident about that  because in march of this year  dizzy times reported that new airpods  are expected to launch  in the third quarter which points to  september  and on top of that mark german said in  may that airpods 3 with a pro looking  design  will launch later this year and what  better time  than alongside the iphones and about a  week ago  digitimes reported that at least seven  apple suppliers  have kicked off component shipments for  upcoming apple products like the apple  watch  iphone and the 3rd gen airpods which  clearly shows  that they're all going to be releasing  at the same time and on top of that  we're expecting the ipad 9 to get  released as well  which can also be revealed at the  september event  so in my opinion it seems a bit too  crowded  to show off the macbook pros at the same  time as everything else  i personally think it makes more sense  for apple to either wait until october  or november for these macbook pros with  a small but  very unlikely chance that apple will  reveal them in  august with a launch in late september  however if apple waits until after the  iphone event  to reveal the new macbook pros this  brings up the question of what apple is  gonna be calling  the new chip that's going into those  macbook pros if they call it the m1x  it might seem weird to do that after  revealing the a15 chip  in the new iphones but it's gonna match  up to their usual naming scheme  and if they end up calling it the m2  chip it's going to be even more weird  because they're going to be the higher  end chips so the big question  is what will apple name the chip that's  going into the redesigned lower end  macbook air  i personally believe the m2 chip will be  very fitting for that lower end macbook  since it's also going to be perfectly  fitting for the 2022 ipad pro  which we just made a video about so in  my opinion apple is either gonna be  calling the new chip going into the  macbook pros  the m1x chip like we previously expected  or they're just gonna go straight to the  m2x  chip and then later when they reveal the  macbook air  they'll give that vm to chip yes that  sounds confusing  so i personally think the biggest bet is  that it's gonna come with the m1x chip  and it's gonna feature the same cores as  the m1 ship  which might seem weird after the a15  comes with newer cores  but hey we can all blame the chip  shortages for that  unless of course apple shocks everyone  at the end of the summer with a surprise  macbook pro reveal which obviously isn't  as likely  but it would surely be awesome to not  wait that long for new max  if you totally disagree with my thoughts  on the macbook pro release date  go ahead and comment your thoughts down  below but if you enjoyed this video  click that circle about to subscribe for  more videos like this one  definitely check out one of those two  videos right there thanks for watching  and we'll see you  in the next one
 

